Package: joinpoint
Type: Package
Title: Trend Analysis by Joinpoint Regression
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Sahar", "Khademioore", email = "sahar.khademi975@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3025-0006"))
Description: Fits joinpoint (segmented line) regression models for trend
    analysis of rates, proportions, counts and other series (Kim et al.
    (2000) <doi:10.1002/(SICI)1097-0258(20000215)19:3%3C335::AID-SIM336%3E3.0.CO;2-Z>).
    Joinpoints are located by an exhaustive grid search (Lerman (1980)
    <doi:10.2307/2346413>) and the number of joinpoints is selected by the
    weighted Bayesian information criterion, BIC, BIC3, modified BIC, data
    dependent selection, the sequential permutation test or a Monte Carlo
    likelihood ratio test. Provides annual percent change (APC) and average
    annual percent change (AAPC) estimates with parametric and empirical
    quantile confidence intervals (Kim et al. (2017) <doi:10.1002/sim.7344>),
    heteroscedastic and autocorrelated error options, Poisson and logistic
    joinpoint models (Czajkowski et al. (2008) <doi:10.1002/sim.3017>),
    covariate adjustment, continuous joinpoints (Hudson (1966)
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.1966.10482198>), jump and comparability ratio
    models, pairwise comparisons of trends (Kim et al. (2004)
    <doi:10.1111/j.0006-341X.2004.00256.x>), clustering of contiguous age
    groups, age adjustment, and 'ggplot2' graphics.
